# Golden/conformance vectors must be byte-identical on every platform.
# Without this, git on Windows checks text files out with CRLF and the
# byte-exact golden comparisons fail (myotis-engine's
# catalog_matches_committed_golden_sample was the first casualty — the Rust
# and Java engines pin their serialization to the committed bytes).
rust/testdata/**/*.json text eol=lf
rust/testdata/**/*.txt text eol=lf
rust/testdata/**/*.bin binary
rust/testdata/**/*.rlp binary
rust/testdata/**/*.ssz binary
rust/testdata/**/*.export binary

# Shell scripts are run by bash on every platform, Git Bash on Windows
# included (rust/repro-env.sh is sourced by the Windows legs; Gradle runs
# rust/build-android.sh), and bash does not read `then\r` as a keyword (#734).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Vendored third-party sources (rust/vendor/ant/VENDORED.md) stay byte for byte upstream's
# on every platform: no line-ending conversion, so scripts/vendor_ant.sh --check compares
# like with like and include_str! embeds the same bytes everywhere. linguist-vendored keeps
# them out of the repository's language statistics.
rust/vendor/** -text linguist-vendored
